{
  "source": "Phase-1 regression set (iter-13/iter-14/iter-16 validation beats): full narrator response documents distilled from three live agent-in-the-loop sessions (session 1: seed 125, log logs/run_125_0.jsonl; session 2: seed 8, the theft-and-arson scenario, log logs/run_8_1.jsonl; session 3: seed 7, the presence-focused session over the st-1 machinery, log logs/run_7_0.jsonl - gitignored runtime artifacts; provenance worklog iter-13/iter-14/iter-16). Each case replays through the REAL mediator cycle (Simulator + Mediator + SceneLedger, cli/mediator.py) - not the validator or the gateway in isolation: the beat-level pins behind the phase-1 exit criterion '0 canon violations per 100 beats' (ROADMAP 2). After iter-14 the corpus pins every validator refusal reason at the beat level (incl. event_type_mismatch, cannot_know), the stale_ref gateway refusal, the full delta vocabulary (established/pinned/retired/no-op), the regen-exhaustion ladder, and both door outcomes (committed success + committed intent_rejected; rebased intents). Session 3 (iter-16, over the iter-15 presence machinery) adds the st-1 acceptance probes: quiet-beat room naming from the entity cards alone, the absent-presence refusal (naming an entity the cards do not carry), arrival-sighting knowledge + directed pair tokens as supported claims, the unseeded pair axis as unverifiable (the honest-verdict law at the pair level), scene-change card follow, the promoted prop riding the card's scene line, and post-rotation cards tracking the watch (KI#46 fixed in the same iteration: the rotation now carries items - the purse no longer lies about its position). Session 4 (iter-17, seed 15 — the crime-cascade session over the presence machinery: 10 beats, 32 supported / 2 refused-and-caught claims, 5 intents fed, 0 canon violations) adds the crime-cascade probes: witnesses present on the cards with the noticed-reach knowledge claimable per witness, the purse carried moving across cards (guard -> player) and riding the flee (KI#46's read-side contract), the blind-witness refusal (a witness who only heard the noise cannot be claimed to have seen the reach), the uninferred purse_missing refusal (the guard cannot know the purse is gone before the inference event), and the rumor_told transfer to the player. The string 'anchor' in expected_event_seq / based_on_event_seq resolves to the anchor the emitted call advertised (the narrator's contract, BRIEF_SPEC 7.1); integers pass through. Expectations: status + note substrings (+ optional last_event_type, log_unchanged vs the emit moment, call_contains on a final emit).",
